<%#
  CloudFormation stack policy paired with data.yml.erb.

  This is NOT a stack template — it's a stack policy applied to the
  `DATA-<rack_env>` stack during create/update. lib/cdo/aws/cloud_formation.rb
  auto-discovers it by deriving the policy filename from the template
  filename (`data.yml.erb` -> `data-policy.yml.erb`) and passes its
  rendered JSON as `stack_policy_body` to the AWS SDK call.

  Effect: protects the `Tableau` Redshift cluster from being replaced or
  deleted by any subsequent stack update. If you intentionally need to
  replace Tableau, this policy must be relaxed first (in the AWS console
  or via aws cli) — otherwise the change will be rejected at apply time.

  There is no separate rake task for this file; it ships with whatever
  `stack:data:start` invocation applies the data stack.
%>
Statement:
- Effect: Allow
  Action: 'Update:*'
  Principal: '*'
  Resource: '*'
- Effect: Deny
  Action: ['Update:Replace', 'Update:Delete']
  Principal: '*'
  Resource: LogicalResourceId/Tableau
